<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Aleksandar Vučić</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">b. <a href="/years/1970">1970</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/21st-century">21st century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Aleksandar Vučić is a Serbian politician who has been President of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbia">Serbia</a> since 2017 after serving as prime minister from 2014. He was information minister under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slobodan-milosevic">Slobodan Milošević</a> and in 2008 co-founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbian-progressive-party">Serbian Progressive Party</a>, which has dominated Serbian politics since 2012. Critics accuse his government of curbing media freedom, and protests against it grew after 2024.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/aleksandar-vucic.jpg" alt="Aleksandar Vučić" width="320" height="438" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Oliver Bunic · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Aleksandar_Vu%C4%8Di%C4%87_2025_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
